.TH MKFS 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mkfs \- build a file system (stub)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfs
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The in-tree
.B mkfs
is a placeholder.
It ignores all of its arguments, prints the line
.PP
.EX
mkfs: stub implementation
.EE
.PP
to standard output, and exits.
It does not open any device and does not write anything.
.PP
To create an ext2, ext3 or ext4 file system, use
.BR mke2fs (8)
(also installed as
.BR mkfs.ext2 )
from the e2fsprogs port.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B mkfs
always exits with status 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsck (8),
.BR mke2fs (8)
.SH BUGS
Not implemented.
Because the exit status is always 0, a script that runs
.B mkfs
cannot tell that no file system was created.
